(# EncoderX-14 Reference Manual) '
() '
(14-bit contactless magnetic absolute angle encoder with I\262C interface) '
() '
(Document ENCX14-RM, revision 1.2) '
() '
(NOTICE: THE ENCODERX-14 IS A FICTIONAL COMPONENT.) '
() '
(This manual was written for the ChronoSight project as an original) '
(reference document. It describes an imaginary part. No real product, vendor) '
(or datasheet is reproduced or paraphrased here. Any resemblance of register) '
(names, values or behaviour to a real device is coincidental. Do not use this) '
(document to design real hardware.) '
() '
(Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International \(CC-BY-4.0\).) '
(You may share and adapt this document for any purpose, provided you give) '
(appropriate credit \("EncoderX-14 Reference Manual, ChronoSight project,) '
(CC-BY-4.0"\), link to the licence, and indicate if changes were made.) '
(Licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/) '
() '
(Contents at a glance) '
() '
(  Part 1  Overview ........................................ pages 4-8) '
(  Part 2  Electrical characteristics ...................... pages 9-14) '
(  Part 3  Package and mechanical .......................... pages 15-22) '
(  Part 4  Signal chain and noise .......................... pages 23-27) '
(  Part 5  Register map .................................... pages 28-36) '
(  Part 6  I\262C protocol .................................... pages 37-42) '
(  Part 7  Configuration and start-up ...................... pages 43-46) '
(  Part 8  Application: servo control loops ................ pages 47-50) '
(  Part 9  Diagnostics and fault handling .................. pages 51-54) '
(  Part 10 Reliability ..................................... pages 55-56) '
(  Part 11 Errata .......................................... pages 57-59) '
(  Part 12 Glossary and licence ............................ page 60) '
() '
(The most frequently referenced items are:) '
() '
(  - Register CONF2 and the FILT[2:0] noise filter ......... page 31) '
(  - Output noise versus FILT setting \(table 31-2\) ......... page 31) '
(  - Read latency and phase lag \(table 12-1\) ............... page 12) '
(  - Errata E-3: CONF2 cleared by every reset .............. page 58) '
ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 202.5 36 Td (ENCX14-RM rev 1.2    CC-BY-4.0    page 1 of 60) Tj ET
