stream
BT /F1 9 Tf 11 TL 54 740 Td
(# 8 Ordering information) '
() '
(  Part number          Package   Temperature        Packing) '
(  ENCX14-S8-T          SOIC-8    -40 to +125 \260C     Tape and reel, 2500) '
(  ENCX14-S8-B          SOIC-8    -40 to +125 \260C     Tube, 100) '
(  ENCX14-EVB           Board     0 to +70 \260C        Evaluation board) '
() '
(## 8.1 Device marking) '
() '
(  Line 1:  X14) '
(  Line 2:  YWW \(year digit, week number\)) '
(  Line 3:  Lot code, 4 characters) '
() '
(## 8.2 Silicon revisions) '
() '
(  REV register \(0x01\)   Marking suffix   Notes) '
(  0xA1                  none             First production silicon) '
(  0xA2                  "B"              E-1 and E-2 corrected) '
() '
(Errata E-3, E-4 and E-5 apply to both revisions. See page 57.) '
() '
(## 8.3 Evaluation board) '
() '
(The ENCX14-EVB carries the encoder, a magnet holder with a 6 mm x 2.5 mm) '
(NdFeB magnet, a 3.3 V regulator, I\262C pull-ups \(2.2 kOhm\) and a 2.54 mm) '
(header for a host. Jumper J1 selects the I\262C address. Jumper J2 inserts a) '
(10 Ohm resistor in series with VDD so that brown-out behaviour can be) '
(reproduced with a bench supply.) '
() '
(## 8.4 Related documents) '
() '
(  - ENCX14-AN01  Magnet and air gap selection) '
(  - ENCX14-AN02  Servo loop design with the EncoderX-14) '
(  - ENCX14-ER    Errata sheet \(the content is included on pages 57-59\)) '
() '
(All related documents are fictional and listed for completeness only.) '
ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 202.5 36 Td (ENCX14-RM rev 1.2    CC-BY-4.0    page 8 of 60) Tj ET
endstream
