stream
BT /F1 9 Tf 11 TL 54 740 Td
(# 14 I\262C AC timing) '
() '
(Table 14-1. I\262C AC timing.) '
() '
(  Parameter                  Symbol    Fm \(400 kHz\)    Fm+ \(1 MHz\)    Unit) '
(                                       Min     Max     Min     Max) '
(  SCL clock frequency        fSCL      0       400     0       1000   kHz) '
(  Hold time START            tHD;STA   0.6             0.26           \265s) '
(  SCL low period             tLOW      1.3             0.5            \265s) '
(  SCL high period            tHIGH     0.6             0.26           \265s) '
(  Setup time repeated START  tSU;STA   0.6             0.26           \265s) '
(  Data hold time             tHD;DAT   0               0              \265s) '
(  Data setup time            tSU;DAT   100             50             ns) '
(  Rise time SDA, SCL         tr                300             120    ns) '
(  Fall time SDA, SCL         tf                300             120    ns) '
(  Setup time STOP            tSU;STO   0.6             0.26           \265s) '
(  Bus free time              tBUF      1.3             0.5            \265s) '
() '
(## 14.1 Transfer durations) '
() '
(A 3-byte burst read from STATUS \(page 40\) consists of the write address) '
(byte, the register pointer byte, a repeated START, the read address byte) '
(and 3 data bytes: 6 bytes with acknowledgements, 54 clock cycles plus the) '
(START, repeated START and STOP conditions.) '
() '
(  Bus speed     Burst read time) '
(  100 kHz       540 \265s) '
(  400 kHz       135 \265s) '
(  1 MHz         54 \265s) '
() '
(## 14.2 Clock stretching) '
() '
(The device never stretches the clock. The host may use any clock frequency) '
(up to the limit of the selected mode.) '
() '
(## 14.3 General call) '
() '
(The device ignores the general call address \(0x00\).) '
ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 200.25 36 Td (ENCX14-RM rev 1.2    CC-BY-4.0    page 14 of 60) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
