stream
BT /F1 9 Tf 11 TL 54 740 Td
(# 15 Pinout) '
() '
(  SOIC-8, top view) '
() '
(            +----v----+) '
(     VDD  1 |o        | 8  SDA) '
(     GND  2 |         | 7  SCL) '
(    TEST  3 |         | 6  ADDR) '
(      NC  4 |         | 5  NC) '
(            +---------+) '
() '
(Table 15-1. Pin functions.) '
() '
(  Pin   Name   Type      Function) '
(  1     VDD    Supply    3.3 V supply. Decouple with 100 nF + 4.7 \265F.) '
(  2     GND    Supply    Ground.) '
(  3     TEST   Input     Factory test. Tie to GND.) '
(  4     NC     -         Not connected. Leave open or tie to GND.) '
(  5     NC     -         Not connected. Leave open or tie to GND.) '
(  6     ADDR   Input     I\262C address select, sampled at reset \(page 13\).) '
(  7     SCL    Input     I\262C clock, open-drain bus.) '
(  8     SDA    I/O       I\262C data, open-drain.) '
() '
(## 15.1 Sensor centre) '
() '
(The centre of the Hall array is in the centre of the package body, within) '
(\2610.1 mm. Use the package outline, not the pin row, to place the magnet axis) '
(\(page 21\).) '
() '
(## 15.2 Direction of rotation) '
() '
(Looking at the top of the package, with DIR = 0 \(default\), the angle code) '
(increases when the magnet rotates clockwise. Setting CONF2.DIR = 1 reverses) '
(the direction \(page 32\).) '
() '
(Important: because DIR lives in CONF2, a brown-out reset also returns DIR to) '
(0 \(page 58\). A host that relies on DIR = 1 will see the direction reverse) '
(after a brown-out. In a position loop this turns negative feedback into) '
(positive feedback. Prefer to handle direction in host software, or rewrite) '
(CONF2 after every reset \(page 45\).) '
ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 200.25 36 Td (ENCX14-RM rev 1.2    CC-BY-4.0    page 15 of 60) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
