(# 16 Package dimensions \(SOIC-8\)) '
() '
(  Top view                         Side view) '
() '
(     |<-- D = 4.90 -->|) '
(     +----------------+  ---          +----------------+   ---) '
(     |o               |   ^           |                |    | A = 1.75 max) '
(     |                |   E1 = 3.90   +-+--+--+--+--+--+   ---) '
(     |       +        |   v             |  |  |  |  |  A1 = 0.10 to 0.25) '
(     |  \(Hall centre\) |  ---) '
(     +----------------+) '
(       e = 1.27 pitch) '
() '
(Table 16-1. SOIC-8 dimensions \(mm\).) '
() '
(  Symbol   Description                         Min     Nom     Max) '
(  A        Total height                                        1.75) '
(  A1       Standoff                            0.10            0.25) '
(  b        Lead width                          0.31            0.51) '
(  D        Body length                         4.80    4.90    5.00) '
(  E        Width across leads                  5.80    6.00    6.20) '
(  E1       Body width                          3.80    3.90    4.00) '
(  e        Lead pitch                                  1.27) '
(  L        Foot length                         0.40            1.27) '
(  dZ       Hall array depth below top surface          0.30) '
() '
(## 16.1 Hall array position) '
() '
(The Hall array is centred in the body in both x and y within \2610.10 mm, and) '
(sits 0.30 mm below the top surface of the mould compound. Add 0.30 mm to the) '
(mechanical air gap to obtain the magnetic air gap.) '
() '
(## 16.2 Recommended land pattern) '
() '
(  Pad width 0.60 mm, pad length 1.55 mm, pad row pitch 5.40 mm,) '
(  pad pitch 1.27 mm.) '
() '
(Keep the area under the package free of copper pours on the top layer to) '
(avoid eddy-current effects at high rotational speed.) '
ET
BT /F1 7.5 Tf 200.25 36 Td (ENCX14-RM rev 1.2    CC-BY-4.0    page 16 of 60) Tj ET
